X-WR-CALNAME:Goal 5 km - Amsterdamse Bos parkrun training
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goal5kmamsterdamsebosparkrun-w1-s0-rest@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T193326Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270426
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270427
SUMMARY:COMPLETE REST
DESCRIPTION:COMPLETE REST. Walk if you want to move.\n\nWeek 1 of 19 - Re
 covery\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.\nRACE WEEK +1. Four day
 s COMPLETE rest\, then two 30 min walks. Nothing else. The research band
  for 70.3 recovery is 14-28 days\, and the failure mode is starting the 
 next block on the fitness you had before the taper.\n131 days to Goal 5 
 km - Amsterdamse Bos parkrun.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goal5kmamsterdamsebosparkrun-w2-s0-long@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T193326Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270502
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270503
SUMMARY:▲ LONG RUN 5 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic volume is…
DESCRIPTION:LONG RUN 5 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic volume is the lever - t
 he fastest runners get there on Zone 1 km\, not on intervals.\n\nWeek 2 
 of 19 - Recovery\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volume.\nKeep HR unde
 r 150. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nZone 2 ONLY\, HR under 145. No quali
 ty of any kind. Ten to twenty-four days of easy is the protocol\; traini
 ng hard here only lengthens recovery.\n125 days to Goal 5 km - Amsterdam
 se Bos parkrun.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:goal5kmamsterdamsebosparkrun-w2-s1-push@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260909T193326Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270503
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270504
SUMMARY:Strength UPPER (40 min)
DESCRIPTION:Strength UPPER - push and pull as one session\, 40 min. Does 
