SUMMARY:▲ LONG RUN 10 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic volume is…
DESCRIPTION:LONG RUN 10 km\, HR under 155. Aerobic volume is the lever - 
 the fastest runners get there on Zone 1 km\, not on intervals.\n\nWeek 4
  of 19 - Ramp\nKeep HR under 150. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nTHE BLOCK
  STARTS. Run frequency is the single biggest change: 3 runs a week was y
 our ceiling all season because three swims and three bikes ate the slots
 . Now 4\, going to 6. Frequency first\, then volume\, then intensity - i
 n that order.\n111 days to Goal 5 km - Amsterdamse Bos parkrun.
